# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 as a dependency
- Used pnpm package manager (as indicated by the workspace configuration)
- Updated pnpm-lock.yaml to lock dependencies

### 2. Analytics Configuration
**Modified: src/App.tsx**
- Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/react`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the WouterRouter wrapper
- Placement ensures analytics tracks all route changes across the application

### 3. Verification Steps Completed
- ✅ TypeScript type checking passed (`pnpm run typecheck`)
- ✅ Production build completed successfully (`pnpm run build`)
- ✅ No linting errors introduced
- ✅ Lock file updated correctly

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), the Analytics component was added to the root App component. This is the recommended approach for React/Vite applications.

The component is placed at the root level to ensure:
- All page views are tracked automatically
- Route transitions are captured
- Performance metrics are collected across the entire application

## Next Steps for Deployment

To activate analytics in production:
1. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard under Analytics
2. Deploy the application using `vercel deploy`
3. Verify analytics are working by checking for network requests to `/<unique-path>/view` in the browser's Network tab after deployment

Analytics data will appear in the Vercel dashboard once user visits accumulate.
